---
layout: layouts/base.njk
---
{% from "macros/box.njk" import box %}

{% call box("■ Welcome") %}
<p>Welcome to <b>matilyn.moe</b>! This is a personal site for projects, build notes and things I find interesting.
Pages are written to be read slowly, and most of them have far more detail than they need.</p>
<p class="note">※ This layout was designed for a 1024px-wide screen. It scales up proportionally on larger monitors and switches to a stacked layout on phones.</p>
{% endcall %}

{% call box("■ Projects") %}
<table class="grid">
  <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Status</th><th>Updated</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for p in projects %}
    <tr>
      <td><b>{{ p.name }}</b><br><span class="small">{{ p.desc }}</span></td>
      <td>{{ p.category }}</td>
      <td><span class="status status-{{ p.status }}">{{ p.status }}</span></td>
      <td class="nowrap">{{ p.updated | ymd }}</td>
    </tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="more"><a href="/projects/">» view all projects</a></p>
{% endcall %}

<div class="two-up">
{% call box("■ About this site") %}
<p>Hand-written HTML and CSS, built with Eleventy. No JavaScript frameworks, no tracking.
The 1px borders and dense text are on purpose.</p>
{% endcall %}
{% call box("■ Currently") %}
<dl class="kv">
  <dt>Printing</dt><dd>Solvent drip tray</dd>
  <dt>Reading</dt><dd>—</dd>
  <dt>Listening</dt><dd>—</dd>
</dl>
{% endcall %}
</div>
